      {
        "id": 92267,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-19T19:25:43.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Why would playing the One-Shot not immediately produce its effect, before anything else happens?&nbsp; I still don't see why it should function differently from activating a Power.&nbsp; There's no \"counterspell\" in this game; you don't need to pause after playing a card to see whether it was actually successfully played, because nothing can prevent it.&nbsp; So why would you pause after the card is played before resolving its effects?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This is pretty close to my thoughts on it.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Our ideas of timing are a concensus, not official. &nbsp;I honestly can't see how one-shots (as worded in the Manual) and the text of Informant aren't simultaneous. &nbsp;With it being officially stated that there are not different speeds, or chains of cards in this game I don't see how it can happen,</p>\n<p>unless</p>\n<p>Our entire notion of timing is wrong.</p>\n<p>So I'm going to throw it out and see where that leads.</p>",
