      {
        "id": 92269,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-19T19:33:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well there are \"chains\" in the sense that, say, Ambuscade can play bunches of his \"shuffle the deck and play another card\" cards and they'll all pile up in play, not quite finished resolving until they're all done.&nbsp; So I can maybe see the possibility of a scenario where, if the Informant had to wait for the one-shot to resolve before she played her card, she might have to wait a long time for the stack to clear (say, if AZ played Onboard Module Installation, drew and played Hoarfire to kill her, she'd die before responding to either of the cards played, instead of responding immediately to both of them).&nbsp; I'm guessing that this is the reason why it's not allowed, though I still disagree.</p>",
        "post_number": 75,
